0 @N1828@ NOTE The 1930 Census determined the population of the United States to b
1 CONC e 122,775,046. This is an increase of almost 16 percent over the 1920 Ce
1 CONC nsus, which reported a population of 106,021,537. This was the 15th dece
1 CONC nnial census conducted in the United States under authority granted by A
1 CONC rticle I, Section 2 of the United States Constitution. It was conducte
1 CONC d in April 1930, except in Alaska, where it was conducted in late 1929
1 CONC . Until 2012 the 1930 Census is the latest available to the public, du
1 CONC e to 72-year privacy laws. It is based on actual counts of persons livin
1 CONC g in residential structures.
