0 @N1840@ NOTE Before vital records were recorded by city, county, or state govern
1 CONC ments, local newspapers often published articles listing or detailing th
1 CONC ese events. Obituaries contain vital and biographical information on th
1 CONC e decedent but also on his or her family and relatives.Society pages beg
1 CONC an as a way to entice readers with gossip and news about the wealthy an
1 CONC d famous but soon evolved to cover the goings-on of “average” citizens
1 CONC . An incredible array of information can be discovered in these societ
1 CONC y pages or sections from seemingly mundane notices and reports on event
1 CONC s such as parties, job changes, hospital stays, and social visits by fri
1 CONC ends or relatives. These pages are a source of historical events that ar
1 CONC e unlikely to exist in any other record.Coverage and completeness in thi
1 CONC s collection varies by title.
