0 @N1908@ NOTE Federal census takers were asked to record information about ever
1 CONC y person who was in each household on the census day. A census taker mig
1 CONC ht have visited a house on a later date, but the information he collecte
1 CONC d was supposed to be about the people who were in the house on the censu
1 CONC s day. The basic census enumeration unit was the county. Each county wa
1 CONC s divided into enumeration districts, one for each enumerator. The compl
1 CONC eted forms were sent to the Commerce Department's Census Office in Washi
1 CONC ngton, D.C.Federal censuses are usually reliable, depending on the knowl
1 CONC edge of the informant and the care of the census enumerator. Informatio
1 CONC n may have been given to a census taker by any member of the family or b
1 CONC y a neighbor. Some information may have been incorrect or deliberately f
1 CONC alsified.
