0 @N2020@ NOTE From the late 17th century until 1857 the Church of Ireland (then t
1 CONC he State Church) was accountable for testamentary administration. An est
1 CONC ate was administered based on if the deceased had made a will, the valu
1 CONC e of the property they owned, and whether their property was located i
1 CONC n more than one diocese. The records in this collection originated fro
1 CONC m the following Church of Ireland Dioceses: Diocese of Armagh, Diocese o
1 CONC f Clogher, Diocese of Connor, Diocese of Derry, Diocese of Down, Dioces
1 CONC e of Dromore and The Diocese of Kilmore. After this point, responsibilit
1 CONC y for the administration of probate in Northern Ireland was transferre
1 CONC d to the state. This collection contains public sector information licen
1 CONC sed under the Open Government License v3.0.
